<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Performance | Wit's Blog</title><link>https://witsblog.github.io/tag/performance/</link><atom:link href="https://witsblog.github.io/tag/performance/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>Performance</description><generator>Wowchemy (https://wowchemy.com)</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0700</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://witsblog.github.io/media/icon_hu66cf44b0d2eab4dae9de00f68d847da7_1567_512x512_fill_lanczos_center_3.png</url><title>Performance</title><link>https://witsblog.github.io/tag/performance/</link></image><item><title>Debugging the 7-Day Spark Job</title><link>https://witsblog.github.io/post/083_spark_gc_starvation/</link><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0700</pubDate><guid>https://witsblog.github.io/post/083_spark_gc_starvation/</guid><description>&lt;br>
&lt;h2 id="the-incident-from-3-hours-to-7-days">The Incident: From 3 Hours to 7 Days&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Our central Spark ingestion pipeline feeds user-defined feature tables into our Feature Store, powering over 100+ production ML models. It is built to scale to
support data science and business users across teams as our feature platform grows.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The job used to take about 3–4 hours. Then it went up to 4 days. Recently, it ran for over 7 days and never finished.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure id="figure-job-duration-over-60-days--not-a-slow-regression-but-a-sharp-performance-drop">
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/01.png" alt="Job duration over 60 days — Not a slow regression, but a sharp performance drop" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;figcaption>
Job duration over 60 days — Not a slow regression, but a sharp performance drop
&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Initial triage checklist:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Did we deploy a code change?&lt;/strong> No. Same commit, same configs.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Did data volume surge?&lt;/strong> No. Row count and data size didn&amp;rsquo;t significantly increase. (I
previously wrote a &lt;a href="https://witsblog.github.io/post/073_data_monitoring/">library&lt;/a> which monitors just exactly this.)&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Is the cluster unhealthy?&lt;/strong> No. Other teams&amp;rsquo; Spark jobs finished normally.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Is the Feature Store throttling?&lt;/strong> No. Write latency and error rate were flat.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Did the job fail with an error?&lt;/strong> No stack traces, no OOM errors, no non-zero exit codes. It just ran forever.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>The Spark UI show active execution:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure id="figure-active-jobs">
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/02.png" alt="Active Jobs" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;figcaption>
Active Jobs
&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Out of 40 tasks, 39 finished in seconds. 1 task however failed 177 times and kept retrying. Every task failure logged:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">ExecutorLostFailure (executor ... exited unrelated to the running tasks)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">Reason: Executor killed by driver.
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>
&lt;figure id="figure-executors-errors">
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/03.png" alt="Executor&amp;#39;s errors" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;figcaption>
Executor&amp;rsquo;s errors
&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The driver logs showed a heartbeat timeout every ~20 minutes:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">Removing executor ... with no recent heartbeats: 149645 ms exceeds timeout 120000 ms
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>So the driver kept killing executors in an infinite loop.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/04.png" alt="" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/05.png" alt="" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The job already had 16 GB per executor. The tempting fix, throwing hardware and memory at it (&lt;em>this will surely help 🤞&lt;/em>):&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">--executor-memory 32g --num-executors &lt;span class="m">100&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>No. This doesn&amp;rsquo;t help—it blows up the cloud bill 💵. As we will see, more executors do nothing when only one task has data. More memory only buys time before an unbounded heap fills up again.&lt;/p>
&lt;br>
&lt;h2 id="business-impact">Business Impact&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>The job runs every few hours to update online features. When it stalls, 100+ production models score on stale data, directly hitting pricing predictions.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The goal was to get runtime back under an hour by fixing the real root cause once and for all.&lt;/p>
&lt;br>
&lt;h2 id="investigation">Investigation&lt;/h2>
&lt;h3 id="1-the-parquet-midpoint-trap">1) The Parquet Midpoint Trap&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>The input was a single ~246 MiB Parquet file. Calling &lt;code>df.rdd.getNumPartitions&lt;/code> returned 40, so Spark launched 40 tasks. But per-task metrics made no sense:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/06.png" alt="" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>One task read all &lt;strong>45,876,936&lt;/strong> rows. The other 39 tasks read 0 bytes and finished immediately.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Why?&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Parquet files store data in &lt;strong>row groups&lt;/strong>, which form the unit of work for
Parquet readers.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Spark doesn&amp;rsquo;t seem know the total number of row groups when it plans. Getting
it would mean opening every file and seeking to the end of each one for its
footer. For multiple files on object storage like AWS S3, that can take time.
I assume that&amp;rsquo;s the trade Spark made.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Instead, when Spark plans file splits, it calculates byte ranges based on file metadata via &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/v3.3.4/sql/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/execution/datasources/FilePartition.scala#L86-L97" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&lt;code>FilePartition.maxSplitBytes&lt;/code>&lt;/a>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">maxSplitBytes&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sparkSession&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">SparkSession&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">selectedPartitions&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Seq&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">PartitionDirectory&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">])&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Long&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">defaultMaxSplitBytes&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">sparkSession&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sessionState&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">conf&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">filesMaxPartitionBytes&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1">// 128 MiB
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">openCostInBytes&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">sparkSession&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sessionState&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">conf&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">filesOpenCostInBytes&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1">// 4 MiB
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">minPartitionNum&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">sparkSession&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sessionState&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">conf&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">filesMinPartitionNum&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">getOrElse&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sparkSession&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">leafNodeDefaultParallelism&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1">// 40
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">totalBytes&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">selectedPartitions&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">flatMap&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">files&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">map&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">getLen&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">+&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">openCostInBytes&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)).&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sum&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">bytesPerCore&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">totalBytes&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">/&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">minPartitionNum&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="nc">Math&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">min&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">defaultMaxSplitBytes&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Math&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">max&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">openCostInBytes&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">bytesPerCore&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">))&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>Each byte range is assigned to 1 task.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The actual read parallelism reckoning comes at read time, when Spark passes a task&amp;rsquo;s byte range to the Parquet reader in &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/v3.3.4/sql/core/src/main/java/org/apache/spark/sql/execution/datasources/parquet/SpecificParquetRecordReaderBase.java#L94-L101" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&lt;code>SpecificParquetRecordReaderBase.initialize&lt;/code>&lt;/a>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-java" data-lang="java">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="n">ParquetReadOptions&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">options&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">HadoopReadOptions&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">builder&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">configuration&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">,&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">file&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">)&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">withRange&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">split&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">getStart&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(),&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">split&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">getStart&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">()&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">+&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">split&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">getLength&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">())&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="c1">// &amp;lt;-- the whole story&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">build&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">();&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>At read time, &lt;code>parquet-java&lt;/code> determines which task owns a row group using a midpoint test in &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/blob/apache-parquet-1.12.2/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/format/converter/ParquetMetadataConverter.java#L1284-L1287" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&lt;code>ParquetMetadataConverter.filterFileMetaDataByMidpoint&lt;/code>&lt;/a>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-java" data-lang="java">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="kt">long&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">midPoint&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">startIndex&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">+&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">totalSize&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">/&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">2&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w">&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">if&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">filter&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">contains&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">midPoint&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">))&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">{&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">newRowGroups&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="na">add&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">rowGroup&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">);&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w">&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">}&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>A task only reads a row group if its byte range covers the row group&amp;rsquo;s midpoint:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/midpoint.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>In our case, the parquet file held exactly 1 row group:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/midpoint_single.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This explains why 1 task did all the work, even though 40 tasks were allocated.&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="2-the-unbounded-future-buffer">2) The Unbounded Future Buffer&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>The skew explains the imbalance, but it doesn&amp;rsquo;t explain why an executor with a 16 GB can&amp;rsquo;t grind through 45.8 million rows however slowly.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>So I took a few thread dumps from an executor before dying, and all pointed to:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&amp;#34;Executor task launch worker for task 5.260 in stage 809.0&amp;#34; RUNNABLE
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> scala.concurrent.impl.Promise$DefaultPromise.onComplete(Promise.scala:307)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> scala.concurrent.Future.zipWith(Future.scala:457)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> scala.concurrent.Future$.$anonfun$sequence$1(Future.scala:671)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> scala.collection.LinearSeqOptimized.foldLeft(LinearSeqOptimized.scala:126)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> scala.concurrent.Future$.sequence(Future.scala:671)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> featurestore.util.ConcurrentFutureProcessor$.concurrentMap(ConcurrentFutureProcessor.scala:32)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>I tracked it down to &lt;code>concurrentMap&lt;/code> in our shared Feature Store library:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">concurrentMap&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">A&lt;/span>, &lt;span class="kt">T&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">](&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">items&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">TraversableOnce&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">A&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">],&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">maxInFlight&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Int&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">timeout&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Duration&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)(&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">task&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">A&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&amp;gt;&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Future&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">T&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">]&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="o">)(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">implicit&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">ec&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">ExecutionContext&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">List&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">T&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">]&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">futures&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">ListBuffer&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">Future&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">T&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">]]()&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">pendingFutures&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">ListBuffer&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">Future&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">T&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">]]()&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">items&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">foreach&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">item&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&amp;gt;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">future&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">task&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">item&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">futures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">append&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">future&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1">// &amp;lt;-- Appended forever, never drained
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">pendingFutures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">append&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">future&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="c1">// Limit concurrency to maxInFlight
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">if&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">pendingFutures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">size&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">&amp;gt;=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">maxInFlight&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">pendingFutures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">headOption&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">foreach&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nc">Await&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">ready&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">timeout&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">))&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">while&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">pendingFutures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">headOption&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">exists&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">isCompleted&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">))&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">pendingFutures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">remove&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">0&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">if&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">futures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">nonEmpty&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="nc">Await&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">result&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nc">Future&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">sequence&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">futures&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">toList&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">),&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">timeout&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1">// &amp;lt;-- Allocations
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">else&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Nil&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>The bug was subtle:&lt;/p>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>&lt;code>pendingFutures&lt;/code> bounded concurrency to &lt;code>maxInFlight&lt;/code> and drained completed futures properly.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>But &lt;code>futures&lt;/code> was never drained. Every future across all 45.8 million rows was appended into a single list and held in memory.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;code>Future.sequence&lt;/code> made it worse: it runs a &lt;code>foldLeft&lt;/code> calling &lt;code>zipWith&lt;/code>, allocating millions more &lt;code>Promise&lt;/code> objects.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol>
&lt;p>The implementation bounds concurrency, but not memory&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="3-stop-the-world-gc-freezes-the-heartbeat">3) Stop-The-World GC Freezes the Heartbeat&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>The job had no JVM telemetry, so I attached an OpenTelemetry agent to the executors to export JVM metrics to Grafana:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure id="figure-g1-old-generation-climbing-linearly-then-gc-duration-spiking-as-it-saturates">
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="https://witsblog.github.io/images/post/083/07.png" alt="G1 old generation climbing linearly, then GC duration spiking as it saturates" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;figcaption>
G1 old generation climbing linearly, then GC duration spiking as it saturates
&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Old generation heap usage (&lt;code>jvm.memory.used&lt;/code>) constantly climbed at ~700 MiB/min.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Old generation usage after collection (&lt;code>jvm.memory.used_after_last_gc&lt;/code>) didn&amp;rsquo;t drop after GC runs. This means the GC cannot reclaim memory because they were still considered live references by the JVM.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Minor GC pauses escalated to 51.4 seconds per minute, meaning application threads were frozen by stop-the-world pauses for over 86% of the time.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>Spark executors send heartbeats every 10 seconds via a background thread in &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/v3.3.4/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/Heartbeater.scala#L38-L48" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&lt;code>Heartbeater&lt;/code>&lt;/a>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">private&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">heartbeater&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">ThreadUtils&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">newDaemonSingleThreadScheduledExecutor&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">name&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="n">heartbeater&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">scheduleAtFixedRate&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">heartbeatTask&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">initialDelay&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">intervalMs&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">TimeUnit&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nc">MILLISECONDS&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>&lt;mark>A long stop-the-world GC pause freezes all JVM threads, including this heartbeater.&lt;/mark>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>On the driver side, &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/v3.3.4/core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/HeartbeatReceiver.scala#L202-L215" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&lt;code>HeartbeatReceiver&lt;/code>&lt;/a> waits up to 120 seconds. When an executor goes silent, the driver assumes it crashed and evicts it:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">if&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">now&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">-&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">lastSeenMs&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">&amp;gt;&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">executorTimeoutMs&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">logWarning&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s">s&amp;#34;Removing executor &lt;/span>&lt;span class="si">$executorId&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s"> with no recent heartbeats: &amp;#34;&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">+&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="s">s&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="si">${&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">now&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">-&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">lastSeenMs&lt;/span>&lt;span class="si">}&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s"> ms exceeds timeout &lt;/span>&lt;span class="si">$executorTimeoutMs&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s"> ms&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="c1">// Asynchronously kill the executor to avoid blocking the current thread
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">killExecutorThread&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">submit&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">new&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Runnable&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">override&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">run&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">()&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Unit&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Utils&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">tryLogNonFatalError&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">sc&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">killAndReplaceExecutor&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">executorId&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>Which is exactly the log we saw:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">Removing executor 158 with no recent heartbeats: 149645 ms exceeds timeout 120000 ms
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>The driver killed the executor, requested a fresh replacement, handed it the exact same task, and watched it freeze and die again—177 times in a row.&lt;/p>
&lt;br>
&lt;h2 id="the-fix">The Fix&lt;/h2>
&lt;h3 id="1-repartition-by-row-count-not-file-bytes">1) Repartition by Row Count, Not File Bytes&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>When tasks execute per-record asynchronous calls, work volume is driven by row count, not byte size.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Instead of relying on Spark&amp;rsquo;s default byte splitting, we explicitly repartition based on target rows:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">targetRowsPerPartition&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="mi">1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">_000_000&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">partitions&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">math&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">max&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">rowCount&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">/&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">targetRowsPerPartition&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">).&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">toInt&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="n">df&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">repartition&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">partitions&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>This breaks any giant row groups into balanced partitions across all executors.&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="2-stream-with-a-semaphore-backpressure">2) Stream with a Semaphore Backpressure&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>Looking at the call site, the caller only cared about recording failed rows:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">errorRows&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">df&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">mapPartitions&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">rows&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&amp;gt;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">rows1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">rows2&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">rows&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">duplicate&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">implicit&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">ec&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">ExecutionContextExecutor&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">scala&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">concurrent&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nc">ExecutionContext&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">global&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">rowIngestion&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">RowIngestionSingletonStore&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nc">_rowIngestionRegistryId&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)(...)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">try&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="nc">ConcurrentFutureProcessor&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">concurrentMap&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">rows1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">maxInFlight&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">timeout&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">row&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&amp;gt;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">rowIngestion&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">ingestAsync&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">row&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">).&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">map&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">result&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&amp;gt;&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">row&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">result&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">==&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">SendResult&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nc">OK&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">))&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">iterator&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">filterNot&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">_2&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span> &lt;span class="c1">// &amp;lt;-- Discard successful rows anyway
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="c1">&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">map&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">_1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">catch&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">case&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">_:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">TimeoutException&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&amp;gt;&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">rows2&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="o">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="o">}(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">df&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">encoder&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">).&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">rdd&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>There was no reason to buffer 45.8 million futures. I replaced it with a bounded streaming worker using a &lt;code>Semaphore&lt;/code>, sth like:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-scala" data-lang="scala">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">ingestPartitions&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">rows&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Iterator&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">Row&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">],&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">rowIngestion&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">RowIngestion&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">,&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">maxInFlight&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Int&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="o">)(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">implicit&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">ec&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">ExecutionContext&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Iterator&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">Row&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">]&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">failed&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">new&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">ConcurrentLinkedQueue&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="kt">Row&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">]()&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">inFlight&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">new&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">Semaphore&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">maxInFlight&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">pending&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">new&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">AtomicLong&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">1L&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">val&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">done&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="k">new&lt;/span> &lt;span class="nc">CountDownLatch&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="mi">1&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="k">def&lt;/span> &lt;span class="n">onOneDone&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">()&lt;/span>&lt;span class="k">:&lt;/span> &lt;span class="kt">Unit&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="o">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl"> &lt;span class="n">inFlight&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">release&lt;/span>&lt;span class="o">()&lt;/span>
