&lt;h2 id="learnings">Learnings&lt;/h2>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Read parallelism is bounded by row groups:&lt;/strong> Spark calculates split tasks by byte ranges, but Parquet readers assign work by row group midpoint.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>The Generational Hypothesis:&lt;/strong> Most objects die young. Structure code so allocations are consumed and dereferenced immediately, never surviving into Old Generation.&lt;/li>
